From ff0c95a363d7cdb9c3e0d438dc9acf95d87bc921 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Devesh Rai <devesh.rai@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 21:48:24 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] Build the router core for Android

Android has no java.awt, log4j-core, virtual threads or JMX, and the app must not
send usage data.  For the Android build:
- board statistics use a small Rectangle2D.Float of their own
- ConductionArea keeps its java.awt fill cache in an Object field and has a fixed
  serialVersionUID, because board hashing serializes the board, and serialization
  reflects on field and method types
- FRLogger logs to standard output (logcat) through a two-class stand-in for Log4j
- post-load board processing runs on a plain daemon thread
- the analytics client is never created
- javadoc-only imports of GUI classes are dropped, so the core builds without the GUI

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
